Ideas and published methods this code follows (no source files were copied)

- Closed-form critically damped and damped springs (src/spring.js), and the
  spring-based form of inertialization (src/inertialize.js): after Daniel
  Holden's article "Spring-It-On: The Game Developer's Spring-Roll-Call"
  (theorangeduck.com, 2021). The equations and the short variable names
  (j0, j1, eydt) follow the article.
- Inertialization: David Bollo's GDC 2018 talk "Inertialization:
  High-Performance Animation Transitions".
- Soft reach near full extension (src/ik.js): Andy Dunn's "soft IK" method.
- Shape-preserving tangents (src/timeline.js): the Fritsch-Carlson monotone
  cubic interpolation method (1980).
- Easing curves (src/easing.js): the standard shapes from Robert Penner's
  easing equations, in the one-line form commonly listed on easings.net.
- mulberry32 (src/noise.js): public domain (Tommy Ettinger). The integer hash
  uses the MurmurHash3 finaliser constants (public domain, Austin Appleby);
  hashString is FNV-1a (public domain).

three.js (installed by npm): MIT License.
